Third-party material bundled in the ledger app.

Everything below ships in the PWA built from frontend/. There is no in-app
credits screen; this file is the attribution.

Geist and Geist Mono
  Copyright 2024 The Geist Project Authors
  (https://github.com/vercel/geist-font)
  SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 (http://scripts.sil.org/OFL)

  Shipped as the .woff2 files in the built bundle, via the npm packages
  @fontsource-variable/geist and @fontsource-variable/geist-mono, which are
  imported in frontend/src/main.tsx. Each of those packages ships the full
  licence text in its own LICENSE file, under frontend/node_modules.

Pixelarticons
  Copyright (c) 2019 Gerrit Halfmann
  (https://github.com/halfmage/pixelarticons)
  MIT License

  The app takes its icon set from here. The SVG path data is generated into
  frontend/src/components/ui/pixelIcons.ts by
  frontend/scripts/generate-pixel-icons.mjs, from pixelarticons 2.2.0. The npm
  package is a devDependency, so what ships is the path data rather than the
  package.

dither-kit 0.1.0
  https://www.tripwire.sh/dither-kit

  Vendored source under frontend/src/components/dither-kit/, installed with
  `shadcn add https://tripwire.sh/r/bar-chart.json` and then modified in place
  (the changes are listed in that directory's README.md). The registry payload
  itself ships no licence file, but dither-kit is built on EvilCharts
  (https://github.com/legions-developer/evilcharts), which is MIT-licensed:
  Copyright (c) 2026 Gurbinder. The MIT terms (use, modification and
  redistribution permitted with this notice) cover the vendored code.

The JavaScript bundle also links the npm libraries declared in
frontend/package.json. React and React DOM, TanStack Query and TanStack Table,
Tailwind CSS, Motion, clsx and tailwind-merge are all MIT licensed; d3-scale and
d3-shape are ISC.
